  "description": "Same race spirit, more fun built in\nThe Synonym was one of the pioneers of the newschool cross-country movement. With more travel and aggressive geometry, it was built to do more than just chase podiums. Since its debut in 2017, it stood proudly on national XCO podiums, proving that longer and slacker bikes are not slower. In fact, today many of the biggest brands have just started to catch up with that idea...\nNow, the Synonym is back with a fresh twist. A touch more travel up front makes the new Synonym DC even more capable – and more fun – on everyday trails. Still fast, still efficient, but no longer obsessed with the clock. In fact this is the exact setup that several of our employees have in their personal bikes.\nIf you live near trails that do not have chairlift access and like the feeling of a lightweight bike that you can throw around all day long, this could just be the bike that ticks that box.\nMAIN FEATURES Race-winning lightweight carbon frame 120mm rear / 140mm front travel 65° head angle for better descending Fox Factory suspension GX Eagle drivetrain NS Bikes Licence carbon handlebar\nRADICAL, UNPRECEDENTED GEOMETRY\nThe longest, slackest XC bike on the market! No other bike comes even close!!!\nFLEX STAYS\nFlex stays eliminate the need for a pivot in the rear triangle. less weight, more lateral stffness..\nFRAME DESIGN\nBeautiful lines by George Dabrowski. Designer of award winning Rondo bikes.",
